      "kana:hi:wo",
      "kana:hi:n"
    ],
    "prerequisites": [
      "kana-hi-row-r"
    ],
    "note": "A three-cell row, and the only one with leftovers: わ is a normal syllable, を survives only as the object particle (pronounced \"o\"), and ん is a consonant on its own.",
    "order": 10
  },
  {
    "id": "kana-hi-small",
    "title": "Hiragana: small っ, ゃ, ゅ, ょ",
    "script": "hiragana",
    "introduces": [
      "kana:hi:sokuon",
      "kana:hi:small-ya",
      "kana:hi:small-yu",
      "kana:hi:small-yo"
    ],
    "prerequisites": [
      "kana-hi-row-w",
      "kana-hi-row-t",
      "kana-hi-row-y"
    ],
    "note": "Four half-size kana that change the beat rather than adding a sound: っ holds the next consonant, and ゃ/ゅ/ょ fuse with the kana before them. Size is the whole distinction — きや is two beats, きゃ is one.",
    "order": 11
  },
  {
    "id": "kana-hi-small-vowels",
    "title": "Hiragana: the small vowels ぁぃぅぇぉ",
